\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Aggregated throughput under strict hardware thread pinning. SPNED exhibits an extraordinary throughput peak at 16 threads ($\approx \SI {59}{GB/s}$), perfectly saturating a single NUMA node's memory controllers. In contrast, the WebAssembly sandbox is constrained by intra-node atomic lock contention and fails to achieve this theoretical hardware peak.\relax }}{13}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:scalability}{{7}{13}{Aggregated throughput under strict hardware thread pinning. SPNED exhibits an extraordinary throughput peak at 16 threads ($\approx \SI {59}{GB/s}$), perfectly saturating a single NUMA node's memory controllers. In contrast, the WebAssembly sandbox is constrained by intra-node atomic lock contention and fails to achieve this theoretical hardware peak.\relax }{figure.caption.8}{}}
